  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square four panel painting of a mirrored crowd of round cartoon creatures with white horns and teeth, in rainbow washes with thick black outlines.",
    "description": "A square painting made of four wood panels joined in a cross, the seams visible. The image is roughly mirrored left to right: a tall column of red and pink creatures with white horns runs up the centre, flanked by rounded creatures in orange, yellow, lime, teal, blue and lilac. Every creature has a single eye, white horn and tooth shapes, and dots, and the colour is laid in translucent washes that overlap like stained glass, with thick black outlines dividing every form. A purple round creature sits at centre, a blue globe at upper right.",
    "impression": "A crowd folded in half and opened again like a Rorschach test, so every monster has a twin. The symmetry calms the chaos into something ceremonial, a totem of creatures. The translucent washes make it glow like a church window, and the cross of the panel seams reads as part of the design.",
